pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% ONE OFF THE BOUNDARY. Byte-for-byte the proof of `../../add.pbp`, with the rup'd degree
% raised by ONE: -9223372036854775807 instead of -9223372036854775808. The addition's true
% degree is then -9223372036854775808 = i64::MIN exactly, which fits, so the cancellation
% subtraction does not wrap and the derived row `1 x2 >= -9223372036854775808` is the
% trivially true constraint it should be.
%
% This proof is REJECTED by the UNFIXED checker and by the fixed one alike. That is the
% point: it pins the forgery to the WRAP and not to "large numbers confuse the checker".
% One unit of magnitude is the entire difference between a forged
% `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` and a correct refusal.
f 1 ;
rup 1 x1 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775807 ;
pol 2 ~x1 + ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
